(518470, 51121, 9906, '<td valign="top">This looks to be a little overexposed.  Nice composition.  Colors are a little blown out.<br/>TC</td>', 'This looks to be a little overexposed.  Nice composition.  Colors are a little blown out.TC', '2003-12-20 13:35:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(518472, 51104, 9906, '<td valign="top">IMHO the sun draws away from the vehicle.  Or is that the effect you were shooting for?  I like the reflections of the sunset, but believe that if you angled out slightly to get rid of the sun...<br/>TC</td>', 'IMHO the sun draws away from the vehicle.  Or is that the effect you were shooting for?  I like the reflections of the sunset, but believe that if you angled out slightly to get rid of the sun...TC', '2003-12-20 13:38:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(518474, 50699, 9906, '<td valign="top">For this type of shot IMHO you need more OR less motion blur on the car.  You also need LOTS MORE light.  The colors are dull and background is not white.  Did you use two pieces of background material?  There is a line up and down about a quarter of the shot in from right.  Things like this can really harm a shot that is set up as this one is.  Or in other words, the more control YOU have over the environment, the more PERFECT the shot has to be to be recieved well at this site.<br/>TC</td>', 'For this type of shot IMHO you need more OR less motion blur on the car.  You also need LOTS MORE light.  The colors are dull and background is not white.  Did you use two pieces of background material?  There is a line up and down about a quarter of the shot in from right.  Things like this can really harm a shot that is set up as this one is.  Or in other words, the more control YOU have over the environment, the more PERFECT the shot has to be to be recieved well at this site.TC', '2003-12-20 13:41:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(518476, 50390, 9906, '<td valign="top">The lighting here is a bit harsh to fully realize (what I believe) you were trying to achieve here.  Earlier or later in day the light would be more cooperative giving you more control. I like the compositoin, but the light is just too harsh for GOOD b/w contrasts.<br/>TC</td>', 'The lighting here is a bit harsh to fully realize (what I believe) you were trying to achieve here.  Earlier or later in day the light would be more cooperative giving you more control. I like the compositoin, but the light is just too harsh for GOOD b/w contrasts.TC', '2003-12-20 13:43:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(518477, 50476, 9906, '<td valign="top">What I''m seeing is a distracting reflection of the window, and NO VEHICLE.<br/>TC</td>', 'What I''m seeing is a distracting reflection of the window, and NO VEHICLE.TC', '2003-12-20 13:44:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(518478, 50885, 9906, '<td valign="top">In my humble opinion, you would have more power with this shot in color OR with more lighing to help bring out the dark detail.  You lose to much in the dark parts of this shot.  Was it night when you took this?  Did you rely solely on camera flash?  More other lighting would definatly help!<br/>TC</td>', 'In my humble opinion, you would have more power with this shot in color OR with more lighing to help bring out the dark detail.  You lose to much in the dark parts of this shot.  Was it night when you took this?  Did you rely solely on camera flash?  More other lighting would definatly help!TC', '2003-12-20 13:46:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(518479, 50821, 9906, '<td valign="top">Nice simple lines, but the lighting is a little harsh for you to get good B/W contrasts here.<br/>TC</td>', 'Nice simple lines, but the lighting is a little harsh for you to get good B/W contrasts here.TC', '2003-12-20 13:48:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(518480, 50820, 9906, '<td valign="top">This looks like your white balance settings were not quite right or you are under exposed.  Either that or you have different kind of snow clouds then we have in Michigan.  Our snow is white ;-)<br/>TC</td>', 'This looks like your white balance settings were not quite right or you are under exposed.  Either that or you have different kind of snow clouds then we have in Michigan.  Our snow is white ;-)TC', '2003-12-20 13:50:07.000000', NULL, 1),
