(521568, 50379, 14509, '<td valign="top">Please accept my congratulatory wishes. <br/>I had hoped this one would have come in first place, but third place is a great honour. Well done!</td>', 'Please accept my congratulatory wishes. I had hoped this one would have come in first place, but third place is a great honour. Well done!', '2003-12-24 00:37:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(521575, 50716, 15291, '<td valign="top">The composition of this photo killed you right from the very start. Every single problem with this photo is directly related to it''s composition. There was absolutly no thought prosess given to this at all. It looks like a classic point, shoot &amp; go home. I am sorry if I seem overly harsh here but there is just no excuse for this. None at all.</td>', 'The composition of this photo killed you right from the very start. Every single problem with this photo is directly related to it''s composition. There was absolutly no thought prosess given to this at all. It looks like a classic point, shoot & go home. I am sorry if I seem overly harsh here but there is just no excuse for this. None at all.', '2003-12-24 00:38:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(521582, 51201, 4927, '<td valign="top">Damn! Watching my score plummet throughout the week, I was hoping to at least score last place since I was doing so poorly. But alas, I missed that coveted position by two places. :(<br/> <br/>I really liked the shot, and never imagined it would do this poorly. Sure, its not a vehicle in the traditional sense, but in my opinion it still fits the challenge. I wanted to do a different and creative interpretation instead of shooting a car, truck, etc. like everyone else. <br/> <br/>Yes, the title is necessary to help one see the meaning I intended, but does this alone negate the image as meeting the challenge? According to the definition of vehicle, both man and the guns are vehicles which transport things in relation to this challenge. The guns are vehicles which transport bullets to targets. Man pulls the trigger and thus is a vehicle which transports death/destruction to whatever the target is. So, by definition and challenge description man is a vehicle which transports a thing. I suppose I was trying to make a philosophical point with this photo as well. Man has in the past and continues to find new ways of annihilating one another. Man is a vehicle of  violence and death. <br/> <br/>I guess too many people wanted a wheel, foot, or motorized vehicle and anything that is outside of that pre-established construct of vehicle scored low because it had no relation to the challenge in their minds. Thank you to the few who saw this photos relevance to the challenge. Oh well! On the bright side, I guess its pretty much upward mobility from here, no?</td>', 'Damn! Watching my score plummet throughout the week, I was hoping to at least score last place since I was doing so poorly. But alas, I missed that coveted position by two places. :( I really liked the shot, and never imagined it would do this poorly. Sure, its not a vehicle in the traditional sense, but in my opinion it still fits the challenge. I wanted to do a different and creative interpretation instead of shooting a car, truck, etc. like everyone else.  Yes, the title is necessary to help one see the meaning I intended, but does this alone negate the image as meeting the challenge? According to the definition of vehicle, both man and the guns are vehicles which transport things in relation to this challenge. The guns are vehicles which transport bullets to targets. Man pulls the trigger and thus is a vehicle which transports death/destruction to whatever the target is. So, by definition and challenge description man is a vehicle which transports a thing. I suppose I was trying to make a philosophical point with this photo as well. Man has in the past and continues to find new ways of annihilating one another. Man is a vehicle of  violence and death.  I guess too many people wanted a wheel, foot, or motorized vehicle and anything that is outside of that pre-established construct of vehicle scored low because it had no relation to the challenge in their minds. Thank you to the few who saw this photos relevance to the challenge. Oh well! On the bright side, I guess its pretty much upward mobility from here, no?', '2003-12-24 00:40:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(521585, 50379, 10437, '<td valign="top">GRATTIS!!!!!<br/>Nice to see another swede win a ribbon!<br/>Congratulations!</td>', 'GRATTIS!!!!!Nice to see another swede win a ribbon!Congratulations!', '2003-12-24 00:41:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(521642, 51084, 12962, '<td valign="top">I don''t understand why this didn''t place higher.  Composition is great, the monochrome really works well (appropriate for the old-fashioned bicycle), and the winding road leads the eyes to wherever the destination is.  Perhaps trim a little bit at the bottom to take out a little bit more of the road,  equal to the height of the space between the top and the head.  But I am just being petty.  Overall, you pretty much portrayed a very leisurely sport very well.</td>', 'I don''t understand why this didn''t place higher.  Composition is great, the monochrome really works well (appropriate for the old-fashioned bicycle), and the winding road leads the eyes to wherever the destination is.  Perhaps trim a little bit at the bottom to take out a little bit more of the road,  equal to the height of the space between the top and the head.  But I am just being petty.  Overall, you pretty much portrayed a very leisurely sport very well.', '2003-12-24 01:01:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(521664, 51180, 15291, '<td valign="top">Hi OneSweetSin,<br/>              The black &amp; white works really well here. The tonal ranges are just about dead on. Not an easy thing to do with a digital camera. The tight cropping though a bit tight also works here because the child is sitting the ride is finished. I must say it is not often you see a photo that captures two completely different elements, 1) The sled meeting the Travel challange &amp; 2) an excellent Portrait to boot. Well done !. What also works here is the soft focus in the face of the child it gives the viewer a sence of crisp cold air. The only thing I can see in the photo is his left arm from just below the shoulder to the elbow gets lost in the snow. This however I do not beleave is any fault of yours, It seems the angle of light, arm &amp; snow just blend it all together. Over all this is a photo you should be very proud of a job very well done ! <br/> <br/>Frankie</td>', 'Hi OneSweetSin,              The black & white works really well here. The tonal ranges are just about dead on. Not an easy thing to do with a digital camera. The tight cropping though a bit tight also works here because the child is sitting the ride is finished. I must say it is not often you see a photo that captures two completely different elements, 1) The sled meeting the Travel challange & 2) an excellent Portrait to boot. Well done !. What also works here is the soft focus in the face of the child it gives the viewer a sence of crisp cold air. The only thing I can see in the photo is his left arm from just below the shoulder to the elbow gets lost in the snow. This however I do not beleave is any fault of yours, It seems the angle of light, arm & snow just blend it all together. Over all this is a photo you should be very proud of a job very well done !  Frankie', '2003-12-24 01:21:03.000000', NULL, 0),
