(522319, 50558, 10546, '<td valign="top">First of all, I would like to thank Nuno Mendonça (therainstorm), for all the help he gave me. Thanks, I owe one!<br/> <br/>To the guy who voted the only "2": I''ll get your name soon, so my revenge is coming.... ehehe (just kidding!)<br/> <br/> <br/>Thanks everyone for your votes! I am very happy with the outcome of this challenge, it''s my best position ever.<br/> <br/>As for the make and model of the car: I don''t know the driver, he was just another guy in a car passing in the day I tried to capture a photo for this challenge. There is another shot of the car where the radiator is more visible but I have no final veredict, so it might be a Mercedes (unlikely), MG, Triumph, Alfa Romeo, Lancia, Fiat or even a Ferrari.<br/> <br/>But it sure looks like a mid 1960 european roadster and was running fine in downtown Lisbon (Portugal).<br/> <br/>Thanks again. Merry Christmas!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2003-12-24 17:55:00.</i></td>', 'First of all, I would like to thank Nuno Mendonça (therainstorm), for all the help he gave me. Thanks, I owe one! To the guy who voted the only "2": I''ll get your name soon, so my revenge is coming.... ehehe (just kidding!)  Thanks everyone for your votes! I am very happy with the outcome of this challenge, it''s my best position ever. As for the make and model of the car: I don''t know the driver, he was just another guy in a car passing in the day I tried to capture a photo for this challenge. There is another shot of the car where the radiator is more visible but I have no final veredict, so it might be a Mercedes (unlikely), MG, Triumph, Alfa Romeo, Lancia, Fiat or even a Ferrari. But it sure looks like a mid 1960 european roadster and was running fine in downtown Lisbon (Portugal). Thanks again. Merry Christmas!', '2003-12-24 13:51:19.000000', '2003-12-24 17:55:00.000000', 0),
(522321, 50558, 10546, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by oskar:</b></div><hr/><i>Well done.<br/> <br/>( I would lika a image stabilzer lens )</i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>No need for a image stabilizer lens (none used), you just follow along the car while shooting in a low speed.</td>', 'Originally posted by oskar:Well done. ( I would lika a image stabilzer lens )  No need for a image stabilizer lens (none used), you just follow along the car while shooting in a low speed.', '2003-12-24 13:53:50.000000', NULL, 0),
