(530720, 51084, 9906, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the kind comments during AND after the challenge!  I''m glad that others liked this photo!  However, when I was making this one, whether or not others would like it was low on my priority list.  This shot I did for MYSELF!  My placing in the contest was and is not an issue in my mind!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-01-05 00:06:49.</i></td>', 'Thanks for the kind comments during AND after the challenge!  I''m glad that others liked this photo!  However, when I was making this one, whether or not others would like it was low on my priority list.  This shot I did for MYSELF!  My placing in the contest was and is not an issue in my mind!', '2004-01-03 15:29:44.000000', '2004-01-05 00:06:49.000000', 0),
(531532, 50379, 15703, '<td valign="top">I am really pleased you agree the movement of the truck doesn''t please as much as you''d hoped. The crisp, cold, gorgeous colours and unusual lighting really make for a stunning totally still picture. I love the mood of your shot - and I''d love it even more if the glaring truck lights weren''t there.</td>', 'I am really pleased you agree the movement of the truck doesn''t please as much as you''d hoped. The crisp, cold, gorgeous colours and unusual lighting really make for a stunning totally still picture. I love the mood of your shot - and I''d love it even more if the glaring truck lights weren''t there.', '2004-01-04 18:08:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(531534, 50656, 15703, '<td valign="top">Like you, I am not keen on the Audi TT. I prefer Toyota Landcruisers!  But your shot is excellent. If it was a dry run for your fantasy of hiring a big studio and shooting a car for real, then go for it. Beautiful lighting, good angle and the car shines in all the right places. I am sure in the big studio you''ll watch out for that bit of unwanted something reflected in the car, here seen especially under the headlamp and towards the wheel arch.</td>', 'Like you, I am not keen on the Audi TT. I prefer Toyota Landcruisers!  But your shot is excellent. If it was a dry run for your fantasy of hiring a big studio and shooting a car for real, then go for it. Beautiful lighting, good angle and the car shines in all the right places. I am sure in the big studio you''ll watch out for that bit of unwanted something reflected in the car, here seen especially under the headlamp and towards the wheel arch.', '2004-01-04 18:20:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(536129, 51082, 9581, '<td valign="top">For a moment I thought it was a real car! Great picture and very creative! I love planes, trains, cars and trucks! I have to add this picture to my favorites you should set this one up to sell as a print!</td>', 'For a moment I thought it was a real car! Great picture and very creative! I love planes, trains, cars and trucks! I have to add this picture to my favorites you should set this one up to sell as a print!', '2004-01-08 10:31:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(537248, 50750, 15900, '<td valign="top">Exellent composition and the positioning of the subjects. Dont worry too much about the ''not white enough snow''. The contrast is there and the ''not white enough snow'' actually gives it a unique characteristic. Great!</td>', 'Exellent composition and the positioning of the subjects. Dont worry too much about the ''not white enough snow''. The contrast is there and the ''not white enough snow'' actually gives it a unique characteristic. Great!', '2004-01-09 10:42:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(537851, 50712, 15703, '<td valign="top">This is very nicely cropped. And the lack of colour really enhances the engineering aspects of the engine.</td>', 'This is very nicely cropped. And the lack of colour really enhances the engineering aspects of the engine.', '2004-01-10 05:15:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(538822, 51065, 14603, '<td valign="top">I appreciate the advice on angles of shot etc. The trouble with this shot was that it wasn`t originally the pic that I was going to enter, <br/>I just liked the designs on the vehicles.My idea was to try to hide the fact that they were vans (ie wheels ,windows, doors etc)but retain enough to identify them (with a bit of work)as vehicles..hence the rear doors and lights.On reflection, what I would like to have done, was to have altered the angle of shot to include more of the advertisement on the other vans and to add to the perspective, but still hide their identity.</td>', 'I appreciate the advice on angles of shot etc. The trouble with this shot was that it wasn`t originally the pic that I was going to enter, I just liked the designs on the vehicles.My idea was to try to hide the fact that they were vans (ie wheels ,windows, doors etc)but retain enough to identify them (with a bit of work)as vehicles..hence the rear doors and lights.On reflection, what I would like to have done, was to have altered the angle of shot to include more of the advertisement on the other vans and to add to the perspective, but still hide their identity.', '2004-01-11 11:55:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(539218, 51157, 14157, '<td valign="top">Sorry about the strange colors. My computer isn''t working properly and I over saturated....... D''OH<br/></td>', 'Sorry about the strange colors. My computer isn''t working properly and I over saturated....... D''OH', '2004-01-12 00:23:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(544259, 50967, 8860, '<td valign="top">Nice angle and viewpoint. I''d have cropped more of the black away at the bottom too as it lifts the shot when there''s less of it.</td>', 'Nice angle and viewpoint. I''d have cropped more of the black away at the bottom too as it lifts the shot when there''s less of it.', '2004-01-15 05:16:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(546046, 51186, 12896, '<td valign="top">i think its a nice pic and good idea.</td>', 'i think its a nice pic and good idea.', '2004-01-16 18:12:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(551042, 51084, 4793, '<td valign="top">What a wonderful photo, the voters must be blind! Your composition with the biker and the curving street makes me feel like I''m riding along with him. This is definately a winner, congratulations on a wonderful capture.</td>', 'What a wonderful photo, the voters must be blind! Your composition with the biker and the curving street makes me feel like I''m riding along with him. This is definately a winner, congratulations on a wonderful capture.', '2004-01-20 22:22:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(552528, 50388, 16188, '<td valign="top">Interestingly shaped feet. :)</td>', 'Interestingly shaped feet. :)', '2004-01-21 15:55:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(553859, 51172, 15703, '<td valign="top">I like this very much. Refreshingly different.</td>', 'I like this very much. Refreshingly different.', '2004-01-22 18:03:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(554796, 50976, 16188, '<td valign="top">I love this.</td>', 'I love this.', '2004-01-23 17:12:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(559058, 50821, 8860, '<td valign="top">Nice, dynamic angle but suffers a little for overexposure. I think mono would work well if all the tones were deeper and showed off that bubbling paint work some more. Nice.</td>', 'Nice, dynamic angle but suffers a little for overexposure. I think mono would work well if all the tones were deeper and showed off that bubbling paint work some more. Nice.', '2004-01-27 14:03:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(560206, 51052, 6999, '<td valign="top">Meant to comment on this at the time, Jon, and never got round to it, and then remembered it yesterday whilst out and about so I''ve come back to find it. Do those noise/too dark comment rile you like they do me - the presumption that you''ve made a mistake, rather than a choice? I liked this a lot, and still do.<br/> <br/>What makes it for me are two particular complementary elements you have going on: the sky disappearing to black top left balances that white car bottom left, and also the darkness of the pile of scrap bottom right: the white car and the scrap also balance each other, which provides great natural framing for the main subject: the crane coming in from the ''vacant'' corner, neatly brings the eye to the main car, which process makes the centred composition work well. <br/> <br/>I guess I''d have tried to reduce the sharpening artefacts around the edges of the crane arm, but in such grainy (noisy!!) work it doesn''t really offend. I guess you knew it was going to get slammed, but I think it''s a very strong shot.<br/> <br/>Ed</td>', 'Meant to comment on this at the time, Jon, and never got round to it, and then remembered it yesterday whilst out and about so I''ve come back to find it. Do those noise/too dark comment rile you like they do me - the presumption that you''ve made a mistake, rather than a choice? I liked this a lot, and still do. What makes it for me are two particular complementary elements you have going on: the sky disappearing to black top left balances that white car bottom left, and also the darkness of the pile of scrap bottom right: the white car and the scrap also balance each other, which provides great natural framing for the main subject: the crane coming in from the ''vacant'' corner, neatly brings the eye to the main car, which process makes the centred composition work well.  I guess I''d have tried to reduce the sharpening artefacts around the edges of the crane arm, but in such grainy (noisy!!) work it doesn''t really offend. I guess you knew it was going to get slammed, but I think it''s a very strong shot. Ed', '2004-01-28 07:46:26.000000', NULL, 0),
